      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"entities\": [{\"id\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"name\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) subject offered table: one row per subject offered in a term within the textbook program scope, with subject identity, offering department/school, responsible faculty, enrollment count, and a flag indicating whether the subject has no course material. Parent of TIP_DETAIL via TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\", \"columns\": {\"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Surrogate key of the TIP subject offered record; joins to TIP_DETAIL.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY\"}, \"TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code in YYYYTT format; joins to ACADEMIC_TERMS/ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\"}, \"IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject has no course material; 'N' means the subject has course materials\"}, \"MASTER_COURSE_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Course number of the master subject\"}, \"MASTER_COURSE_NUMBER_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the master course number\"}, \"MASTER_COURSE_NUMBER_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Description of the master course number\"}, \"MASTER_SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Master subject identifier for clustered subjects\"}, \"MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the master subject identifier\"}, \"COURSE_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Course number of the subject\"}, \"COURSE_NUMBER_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the course number\"}, \"COURSE_NUMBER_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Course number description\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Subject identifier, e.g. '5.01'; joins to TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the subject identifier\"}, \"SUBJECT_TITLE\": {\"desc\": \"Subject title\"}, \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Offering department code; joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE and STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}, \"OFFER_DEPT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Offering department name, e.g. 'Chemistry', 'Mathematics'\"}, \"OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Offering school name\"}, \"RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the faculty member responsible for the subject\"}, \"RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"MIT ID of the responsible faculty member\"}, \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\": {\"desc\": \"Number of students enrolled in the subject; used for enrollment-based rankings and window statistics\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per subject per term in the textbook program\"}, {\"id\": \"TIP_DETAIL\", \"name\": \"TIP_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) detail table linking subjects offered in a term to their course textbook materials: material key, material status (e.g. 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options), ISBN, and record count. Used to determine whether subjects have required textbooks and to count course materials per status.\", \"columns\": {\"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Foreign key to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY\"}, \"TIP_MATERIAL_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Foreign key to TIP_MATERIAL.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY identifying the specific textbook material\"}, \"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Material status key; joins to TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY for decoding. Value domain includes 'RQ' = Required, 'EO' = Electronic options, 'RC' = Recommended, 'PC' = Val-u option, 'BR' = Bookstore recommends, 'CL' = Go to class first, 'NM' = Course has no materials, 'U' = Unknown, and 'NL'/'NS'/'NB'/blank keys with no description. Distinct from LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, which belongs to the library reserve domain.\"}, \"TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code in YYYYTT format; joins to ACADEMIC_TERMS/ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Subject identifier, e.g. '18.01'; joins to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID, SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID\"}, \"ISBN\": {\"desc\": \"ISBN of the textbook material associated with the subject offering\"}, \"RECORD_COUNT\": {\"desc\": \"Number of material records for this subject/material combination; used in material-count statistics\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per subject-material-status combination per term\", \"entity\": {\"columns\": {\"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Material status key; joins to TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY for decoding. Value domain includes 'RQ' = Required, 'EO' = Electronic options, 'RC' = Recommended, 'PC' = Val-u option, 'BR' = Bookstore recommends, 'CL' = Go to class first, 'NM' = Course has no materials, 'U' = Unknown, and 'NL'/'NS'/'NB' = None variants. Distinct from LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, which belongs to the library reserve domain.\"}}}, \"reason\": \"Data verification of TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS shows 12 status values beyond the previously documented 'RQ'/'EO'; enriching the description supports material-status grouping questions such as case dw_2989 (per material status and publisher statistics).\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"name\": \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS department dimension table: academic departments with code, name, full name, school attribution (code and name), budget code, degree-granting flag, and commencement-book names. Joins to subject offering tables via department codes.\", \"columns\": {\"DEPARTMENT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Department code; joins to offering tables' DEPARTMENT_CODE/OFFER_DEPT_CODE and SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Department name, e.g. 'Mathematics', 'Chemistry'\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Full official name of the department\"}, \"SCHOOL_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"School code the department belongs to, e.g. 'E'\"}, \"SCHOOL_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"School name the department belongs to, e.g. 'Engineering'; used for school-level filtering\"}, \"DEPT_BUDGET_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Budget code of the department; used for budget-based ordering/ranking\"}, \"IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the department is degree granting\"}, \"DEPT_NAME_IN_COMMENCEMENT_BK\": {\"desc\": \"Department name as printed in the commencement book\"}, \"SCHOOL_NAME_IN_COMMENCEMENT_BK\": {\"desc\": \"School name as printed in the commencement book\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_NAME_HISTORY\": {\"desc\": \"Historical names of the department\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_LAST_ACTIVITY_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Date of last activity on the department record\"}, \"DLC_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Degree-granting list/committee key\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per academic department\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\", \"name\": \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\", \"desc\": \"SIS course description table: catalog descriptions of courses with department and school attribution, course level (undergraduate/graduate), degree-granting flag, graduate level, CIP program code, and effective from/thru terms. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via COURSE = SUBJECT_CODE/COURSE_NUMBER and to SIS_DEPARTMENT via DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE.\", \"columns\": {\"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Surrogate key of the course description record\"}, \"COURSE\": {\"desc\": \"Course/subject code, e.g. '18'; joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_CODE and COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE\"}, \"COURSE_DESCRIPTION\": {\"desc\": \"Short course description text; its character length is used in description-length statistics\"}, \"COURSE_DESCRIPTION_LONG\": {\"desc\": \"Long-form course description text\"}, \"DEPARTMENT\": {\"desc\": \"Department code offering the course; joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Department name offering the course\"}, \"DEPT_NAME_IN_COMMENCEMENT_BK\": {\"desc\": \"Department name as printed in the commencement book\"}, \"SCHOOL_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"School name offering the course, e.g. 'Engineering'\"}, \"SCHOOL_NAME_IN_COMMENCEMENT_BK\": {\"desc\": \"School name as printed in the commencement book\"}, \"FROM_TERM\": {\"desc\": \"First term the course description is effective from\"}, \"FROM_TERM_DESCRIPTION\": {\"desc\": \"Description of the from-term\"}, \"THRU_TERM\": {\"desc\": \"Last term the course description is effective through\"}, \"THRU_TERM_DESCRIPTION\": {\"desc\": \"Description of the thru-term\"}, \"COURSE_OPTION\": {\"desc\": \"Course option designation\"}, \"COURSE_LEVEL\": {\"desc\": \"Course level code, e.g. 'U' = undergraduate, 'G' = graduate\"}, \"CIP_PROGRAM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Six-digit CIP (Classification of Instructional Programs) program code of the course; joins to CIP.PROGRAM_CODE (current classification, one row per code) and CIP_WITH_VERSION.PROGRAM_CODE (all revision versions)\"}, \"IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the course counts toward a degree\"}, \"DEFAULT_ULTIMATE_DEGREE\": {\"desc\": \"Default ultimate degree awarded for the course\"}, \"GRADAUTE_LEVEL\": {\"desc\": \"Legacy misspelled graduate level column (kept for compatibility)\"}, \"GRADUATE_LEVEL\": {\"desc\": \"Graduate level designation of the course\"}, \"LAST_ACTIVITY_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Date of last activity on the record\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per course description\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1165\", \"name\": \"Library-TIP Matched Subjects by Faculty or Enrollment with Degree-Granting Graduate Department Enrollment Dispersion\", \"desc\": \"For each subject where the responsible faculty MIT ID in the library subject offered table is 928034000 or the number of enrolled students in the tip subject offered table is greater than 5, and where the offer department name in the tip subject offered table is either 'Chemistry' or 'Biology', show the subject title from the library subject offered table, the offer department name from the tip subject offered table, the term code from both tables, the number of enrolled students from both tables, and the minimum number of enrolled students in the tip subject offered table over each master subject ID group. Additionally, for the department offering the subject, show the department name, the range of enrolled students, and the variance of enrolled students in the subjects offered by that department, considering only departments that grant degrees, courses that are at the graduate level, and excluding the Biology department. Present the results ordered by subject title and department name. Do not return any rounded answers.\", \"sql\": \"WITH Subquery1 AS ( SELECT lso.SUBJECT_TITLE, tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, lso.TERM_CODE AS LIBRARY_TERM_CODE, tso.TERM_CODE AS TIP_TERM_CODE, lso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS AS LIBRARY_NUM_ENROLLED, tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS AS TIP_NUM_ENROLLED, MIN(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) OVER (PARTITION BY tso.MASTER_SUBJECT_ID) AS MIN_TIP_NUM_ENROLLED, tso.OFFER_DEPT_CODE FROM LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED lso JOIN TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso ON lso.MASTER_SUBJECT_ID = tso.MASTER_SUBJECT_ID WHERE ( lso.RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID = 928034000 OR tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 5 ) AND tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME IN ('Chemistry', 'Biology') ), Subquery2 AS ( SELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, MAX(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) - MIN(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_range, VARIANCE(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_variance, sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT sd ON tso.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE JOIN SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION scd ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = scd.DEPARTMENT WHERE sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND scd.COURSE_LEVEL = 'G' AND sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '7' GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE ), CombinedResults AS ( SELECT s1.SUBJECT_TITLE, s1.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, s1.LIBRARY_TERM_CODE, s1.TIP_TERM_CODE, s1.LIBRARY_NUM_ENROLLED, s1.TIP_NUM_ENROLLED, s1.MIN_TIP_NUM_ENROLLED, s2.DEPARTMENT_NAME, s2.enrolled_range, s2.enrolled_variance FROM Subquery1 s1 JOIN Subquery2 s2 ON s1.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = s2.DEPARTMENT_CODE ) SELECT SUBJECT_TITLE, OFFER_DEPT_NAME, LIBRARY_TERM_CODE, TIP_TERM_CODE, LIBRARY_NUM_ENROLLED, TIP_NUM_ENROLLED, MIN_TIP_NUM_ENROLLED, DEPARTMENT_NAME, enrolled_range, enrolled_variance FROM CombinedResults ORDER BY SUBJECT_TITLE, DEPARTMENT_NAME;\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"default_granularity\": \"one row per library-TIP matched subject offering per degree-granting graduate department\"}, {\"category\": \"Subject Offering and Student Directory Comprehensive Analysis\", \"default_granularity\": \"one row per department/school enrollment statistic (plus per-school rollup rows), left joined with Mathematics students named Peter\", \"desc\": \"For each department and school, provide the department name, school name, the average, range, and variance of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department, and the total enrolled students, considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with at least one enrolled student. Additionally, for each school, include a grand total for all departments in that school in the format of (null department name, school name, nulls for statistics, and total enrolled students). For students whose first name is 'Peter' and who are in the Mathematics department, also show their last name, email address, student year, and the minimum department budget code in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the student's full name, as well as the department full name and department last activity date. The results include all these columns in the following order: department name, school name, average enrolled students, range of enrolled students, variance of enrolled students, total enrolled students, last name, email address, student year, windowed minimum department budget code, department full name, and department last activity date. Do not return any rounded answers.\", \"id\": \"dw_1350\", \"name\": \"Degree-Granting Department TIP Enrollment Statistics with School Rollups and Math Peter Student Budget Code Windows\", \"sql\": \"WITH inner_cte1 AS ( SELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, sd.SCHOOL_NAME, tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT sd JOIN TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = tso.OFFER_DEPT_CODE WHERE sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS >= 1 ), DepartmentStats AS ( SELECT DEPARTMENT_NAME, SCHOOL_NAME, AVG(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_enrolled_students, MAX(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) - MIN(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS range_enrolled_students, VARIANCE(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS var_enrolled_students, SUM(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS total_enrolled_students FROM inner_cte1 GROUP BY DEPARTMENT_NAME, SCHOOL_NAME ), SchoolRollup AS ( SELECT NULL AS DEPARTMENT_NAME, SCHOOL_NAME, NULL AS avg_enrolled_students, NULL AS range_enrolled_students, NULL AS var_enrolled_students, SUM(total_enrolled_students) AS total_enrolled_students FROM DepartmentStats GROUP BY SCHOOL_NAME ), inner_cte2 AS ( SELECT t1.LAST_NAME, t1.EMAIL_ADDRESS, t1.STUDENT_YEAR, t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME, t0.SCHOOL_NAME, MIN(t0.DEPT_BUDGET_CODE) OVER (ORDER BY t1.FULL_NAME ROWS BETWEEN 3 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING) AS window_column FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT t0 JOIN MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY t1 ON t0.DEPARTMENT_CODE = t1.DEPARTMENT WHERE t1.FIRST_NAME = 'Peter' AND t0.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' ) SELECT ds.DEPARTMENT_NAME, ds.SCHOOL_NAME, ds.avg_enrolled_students, ds.range_enrolled_students, ds.var_enrolled_students, ds.total_enrolled_students, ic2.LAST_NAME, ic2.EMAIL_ADDRESS, ic2.STUDENT_YEAR, ic2.window_column, sd.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME, sd.DEPARTMENT_LAST_ACTIVITY_DATE FROM (SELECT * FROM DepartmentStats UNION ALL SELECT * FROM SchoolRollup) ds LEFT JOIN inner_cte2 ic2 ON ds.DEPARTMENT_NAME = ic2.DEPARTMENT_NAME AND ds.SCHOOL_NAME = ic2.SCHOOL_NAME LEFT JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT sd ON ds.DEPARTMENT_NAME = sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY ds.SCHOOL_NAME, ds.DEPARTMENT_NAME, ic2.LAST_NAME ;\"}], \"not_found\": []}"
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_0488508657324fc29cc64758",
      "name": "semantic_get",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"entities\": [{\"id\": \"concept_subject_offering_facts\", \"name\": \"Subject Offering Fact Tables\", \"desc\": \"Fact tables recording subjects offered per term from different business processes: the course catalog (planned catalog attributes), the registrar's section/subject offering records (actual sections and enrollment), subject-level summaries (final enrollment statistics), the textbook information program (subjects tracked for course materials), and library reserve processing (subjects with library reserve activity). They share subject identity (SUBJECT_ID, TERM_CODE) and department attribution but differ in granularity, enrollment semantics, and available measures.\", \"tables\": [\"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Granularity\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"Subject offering per term/academic year (catalog record, includes section flags)\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"Subject section per term (finest grain, SECTION_ID)\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\": \"Subject per term (rollup of sections)\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\": \"Subject or cluster per term\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"Subject per term within textbook program scope\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"Subject per term within library reserve scope\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Enrollment measures\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"None (catalog attributes only)\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER, SECTION_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER, CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\": \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER, CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\": \"SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER plus first-week/fifth-week and credit/listener enrollment splits\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Unit measures\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"LECTURE_UNITS, LAB_UNITS, PREPARATION_UNITS, DESIGN_UNITS, TOTAL_UNITS, IS_VARIABLE_UNITS\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"None\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\": \"TOTAL_UNITS, LECTURE_UNITS, LAB_UNITS, PREPARATION_UNITS\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\": \"TOTAL_UNITS, LECTURE_UNITS, LAB_UNITS, PREP_UNITS, DESIGN_UNITS\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"None\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"None\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Distinctive attributes\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"HGN_DESC level, GRADE_TYPE/GRADE_RULE, HASS/GIR attributes, IS_OFFERED_* flags, MEET_PLACE (room key), ACADEMIC_YEAR, EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"IS_REPEATABLE_SUBJECT, CLUSTER_TYPE, section flags, FORM_TYPE, EVALUATE_THIS_SUBJECT\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\": \"OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME, COURSE_NUMBER, cluster info at subject level\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\": \"SCHOOL_CODE/SCHOOL_NAME, SUBJECT_GROUP_ID, SUBJECT_OR_CLUSTER, detailed weekly enrollment\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL flag; parent of TIP_DETAIL materials\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"COURSE_NUMBER/COURSE_NUMBER_DESC; parent of LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Department column naming\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"DEPARTMENT_CODE / DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\": \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\": \"DEPARTMENT_CODE / DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\": \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_NAME\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Questions about credit units, grading type/rules, HGN level (undergraduate/graduate), HASS/GIR attributes, or term offering flags (fall/spring/IAP/summer)\": \"Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED; it is the only offering table carrying full catalog attributes.\", \"Questions about actual section-level offerings, repeatability, cluster type, or section flags\": \"Use SUBJECT_OFFERED (section grain); roll up via SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY when subject-level totals are needed.\", \"Questions about final enrollment statistics, weekly enrollment snapshots, credit vs listener counts, subject groups, or school-level unit statistics\": \"Use SUBJECT_SUMMARY.\", \"Questions about textbooks/course materials per subject (required/optional status, ISBN, record counts)\": \"Start from TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (subject scope, IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL) joined to TIP_DETAIL (material rows).\", \"Questions about library reserve materials, reserve counts per subject, or library course numbers\": \"Start from LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED joined to LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.\", \"Questions about subject-level units with offering department/school (e.g. Engineering school enrollment totals by department)\": \"Use SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, which carries both TOTAL_UNITS and OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME.\"}}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_material_programs\", \"name\": \"Course Material and Library Reserve Domain\", \"desc\": \"Tables covering course material provisioning: the Textbook Information Program (TIP) tracking textbook adoption status per subject offering, and library reserve processing tracking catalog items placed on reserve for subjects. They jointly answer questions about which subjects have course materials/textbooks, material status (TIP statuses such as 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options; library statuses such as 'U' Unknown, 'Y' Required Course Material), ISBNs, record counts, and reserve catalog item attributes. The two programs are linked by SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE.\", \"tables\": [\"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"TIP_DETAIL\", \"TIP_MATERIAL\", \"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\", \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG\", \"LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS\", \"LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Business process\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / TIP_DETAIL / TIP_MATERIAL / TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS\": \"Textbook program: subjects tracked for textbook adoption, material rows with status and ISBN, material bibliographic details, status decoding\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED / LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL / LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG / LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS / LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR\": \"Library reserve: subjects in reserve processing, reserve material detail rows, catalog item bibliographic records, status decoding, instructor assignments\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Status semantics\", \"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\": \"12 statuses decoded by TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS: 'RQ' = Required, 'EO' = Electronic options, 'RC' = Recommended, 'PC' = Val-u option, 'BR' = Bookstore recommends, 'CL' = Go to class first, 'NM' = Course has no materials, 'U' = Unknown, plus NULL-description keys 'NL'/'NS'/'NB'/blank\", \"LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\": \"6 statuses decoded by LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS: 'U' = Unknown, 'R' = NULL description, 'N' = Non-Required Course Material, 'O' = Reserve only, 'X' = No Required Textbook, 'Y' = Required Course Material\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Count measures\", \"TIP_DETAIL\": \"COUNT(TIP_MATERIAL_KEY) or RECORD_COUNT for material-count statistics per status/subject\", \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\": \"COUNT(LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY) for reserve catalog item counts per status/subject; LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG.RECORD_COUNTER is a catalog record counter\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Parent-child structure\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED → TIP_DETAIL\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY / SUBJECT_ID links subject rows to material rows\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED → LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL → LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG\": \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY and LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY chain subjects to reserve items\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Questions about required/optional textbooks, ISBNs, or whether subjects have course materials\": \"Use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL flag) with TIP_DETAIL (TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY 'RQ'/'EO').\", \"Questions about library reserve items, reserve counts per subject, or catalog titles/authors\": \"Use LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL joined to LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG, scoped by LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\", \"Questions about enrollment of subjects within the textbook program or library reserve scope\": \"Use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS or LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS respectively; these are program-specific snapshots, not the official SUBJECT_SUMMARY enrollment.\", \"Questions about textbook prices, editions, or publishers\": \"Use TIP_MATERIAL via TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_KEY.\", \"Questions about instructors of courses with reserve materials\": \"Use LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR via LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR_KEY.\", \"Questions about required textbooks, ISBNs, or whether subjects have course materials\": \"Use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL flag) with TIP_DETAIL (TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, e.g. 'RQ' Required).\", \"Questions combining textbook material statuses with library reserve statuses\": \"Join TIP_DETAIL and LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL on SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE, decode each status via its own lookup table, and aggregate each side separately; never equate the two status key columns.\"}}, {\"id\": \"concept_department_dimension\", \"name\": \"Department and School Dimension\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables describing academic departments and their school attribution: the SIS department dimension, the student-facing department lookup, and the SIS administrative department (contact information). They answer questions about department names, full names, school code/name, degree-granting status, budget codes, and department phone numbers, but differ in attribute coverage.\", \"tables\": [\"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\", \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Attribute coverage\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\": \"Richest: DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME, SCHOOL_CODE/SCHOOL_NAME, DEPT_BUDGET_CODE, IS_DEGREE_GRANTING, commencement-book names, DLC key\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\": \"Minimal: code, name, full name, school code/name only\", \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\": \"Administrative contact: department phone area code/number, clearing cost collector\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Degree-granting and school filtering\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\": \"Supports IS_DEGREE_GRANTING and SCHOOL_NAME filters directly\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\": \"Only school code/name attribution, no degree-granting flag\", \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\": \"No school or degree-granting attributes\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Typical join path\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\": \"DEPARTMENT_CODE = offering tables' DEPARTMENT_CODE/OFFER_DEPT_CODE; also joins SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT and SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT.SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\": \"DEPARTMENT_CODE = TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE and other offering department codes\", \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\": \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE = SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Budget/finance attributes\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\": \"DEPT_BUDGET_CODE available for budget-based ranking\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\": \"None\", \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\": \"CLEARING_COST_COLLECTOR\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Questions filtering departments by school (e.g. 'School of Engineering') or degree-granting status\": \"Use SIS_DEPARTMENT; it carries SCHOOL_NAME and IS_DEGREE_GRANTING.\", \"Questions needing only department full name and school name for offering departments (e.g. TIP subject offerings)\": \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT suffices and is the lighter lookup; SIS_DEPARTMENT also works.\", \"Questions needing department phone numbers or administrative contact details\": \"Join SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT via SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE = SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE.\", \"Questions ranking or grouping departments by budget code\": \"Use SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPT_BUDGET_CODE.\"}}, {\"columns\": [\"SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Measure meaning\", \"detail\": \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS is the headcount of students enrolled (present in SUBJECT_OFFERED at section grain, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY at subject grain, and in TIP/LIBRARY program snapshots); SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER is the official subject enrollment number recorded by the registrar (SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY)\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Grain\", \"detail\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS is per section; SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS is per subject per term; SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER is the final subject-level enrollment with weekly/credit/listener breakdowns available in sibling columns\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Program scope\", \"detail\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED and LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED enrollment values are snapshots within the textbook-program and library-reserve scopes respectively and may not cover all subjects\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Questions about official subject enrollment (e.g. 'subject enrollment number greater than 10')\": \"Use SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER.\", \"Questions about number of enrolled students per subject offering or per department totals\": \"Use NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS from SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject grain) or SUBJECT_OFFERED (section grain, needs aggregation).\", \"Questions about enrollment of subjects within the textbook program or library reserve scope\": \"Use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS or LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS respectively.\", \"Questions needing enrollment timing (first week, fifth week) or credit vs listener splits\": \"Use SUBJECT_SUMMARY's SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_FIRST_WEEK / FIFTH_WEEK and *_CREDIT / *_LISTEN columns.\"}, \"desc\": \"Enrollment measure columns across subject offering, summary, textbook-program, and library tables. Two families exist: NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (student headcount snapshots) and SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (official registrar enrollment), at section, subject, or program scope.\", \"id\": \"column_concept_enrollment_measures\", \"name\": \"Enrollment Measures\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"name\": \"Department Name\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\", \"columns\": [\"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT\", \"MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Naming convention\", \"detail\": \"DEPARTMENT_NAME is used by catalog/summary tables (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY), department/course lookup tables, and the student directory (MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY); OFFER_DEPT_NAME is used by offering/program tables (SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED) and denotes the department that actually offers the subject; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR uses the plain column name DEPARTMENT for the course's academic department; SE_PERSON uses ORGANIZATION for the person's organizational unit\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Value format\", \"detail\": \"Catalog, summary, offering, student-directory, and lookup tables store plain department names (e.g. 'Mathematics', 'Chemistry', 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'); LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT stores a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics', '06 - Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'), with some unprefixed values (e.g. 'Architecture'), so it is not directly comparable to plain-name columns without stripping the prefix\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Academic vs HR/organization value domain\", \"detail\": \"Catalog, summary, offering, library, student-directory, and lookup tables share the academic department domain; EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME is the HR organizational unit name and has a different domain (e.g. 'Lincoln Laboratory', 'Department of Physics'), where some values coincide with academic names but many do not, and some carry a 'Department of ...' prefix; SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION holds organizational unit names that may use different naming variants than the academic domain for the same unit (e.g. 'Electrical Engineering-Computer Science' vs the academic 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'), so equality filters across the two conventions must use each table's own variant\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Companion code column\", \"detail\": \"Catalog/summary tables carry DEPARTMENT_CODE joining SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; offering/program tables carry OFFER_DEPT_CODE joining SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE or STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY carries DEPARTMENT (the academic department code) joining SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, which is the reliable join key instead of the name; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR has no department code column, only the prefixed name text; EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY carries DEPARTMENT_NUMBER (HR department number) and SE_PERSON carries no department code, neither joining to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Filtering subjects by department in catalog or summary analysis\": \"Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME or SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME.\", \"Filtering by department in section-level, textbook-program, or library analysis\": \"Use the OFFER_DEPT_NAME column of SUBJECT_OFFERED / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\", \"Joining fact tables to department dimension attributes (school, full name, degree-granting)\": \"Prefer code joins: DEPARTMENT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_CODE = SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; name equality joins are used when codes are unavailable.\", \"Matching departments across a DEPARTMENT_NAME table and an OFFER_DEPT_NAME table\": \"The values are directly comparable (same academic name domain), e.g. joining SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME.\", \"Filtering employees by their HR organizational unit (e.g. names containing 'Department', or HR units like 'Political Science')\": \"Use EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME; do not join it to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, and pair it with DEPARTMENT_NUMBER for HR grouping.\", \"Filtering by department in section-level, textbook-program, or library subject analysis\": \"Use the OFFER_DEPT_NAME column of SUBJECT_OFFERED / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\", \"Filtering library reserve course instructors by academic department or library unit\": \"Use LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT with the prefixed value format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); do not compare it directly to plain department-name columns.\", \"Filtering students by their academic department\": \"Use MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT (code) joined to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE for reliable matching, or MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME for direct name filters; the name shares the academic domain with SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME.\", \"Filtering a person master (SE_PERSON) record by organizational unit such as an academic department\": \"Use SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION with its own naming variant (e.g. 'Electrical Engineering-Computer Science'); do not equate it directly to MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME or SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, which use the academic variant (e.g. 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci').\"}}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_subject_id\", \"name\": \"Subject Identifier\", \"desc\": \"Subject identifier columns shared across catalog, registrar, textbook-program, and library tables. SUBJECT_ID is the cross-domain subject join key in 'CODE.NUMBER' format (e.g. '18.01'); it appears in every subject-related fact table but at different grains and program scopes.\", \"columns\": [\"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID\", \"TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\", \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Format\", \"detail\": \"SUBJECT_CODE + '.' + SUBJECT_NUMBER in all tables, e.g. '18.01'; can be reconstructed via CONCAT(SUBJECT_CODE, '.', SUBJECT_NUMBER)\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Grain difference\", \"detail\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: catalog offering scope, one SUBJECT_ID may repeat across terms/academic years; SUBJECT_OFFERED: section scope, same SUBJECT_ID appears once per section; SUBJECT_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY: subject scope per term, one row per SUBJECT_ID per term; TIP and LIBRARY tables: program scope, SUBJECT_ID present only if the subject is tracked by that program\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Joining textbook materials or library reserves to catalog/summary subject attributes\": \"Match on SUBJECT_ID (plus TERM_CODE when term scope matters).\", \"Joining catalog offerings that only expose SUBJECT_CODE/SUBJECT_NUMBER to SUBJECT_ID-based tables\": \"Reconstruct SUBJECT_ID as CONCAT(SUBJECT_CODE, '.', SUBJECT_NUMBER).\", \"Counting distinct subjects per term/department\": \"Use COUNT(DISTINCT SUBJECT_ID) on a subject-grain table (SUBJECT_SUMMARY or SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY) to avoid section/program duplication.\"}}], \"not_found\": []}"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The precedent dw_1165 gives the exact pattern for range/variance with degree-granting + graduate-level filters. Let me search for precedents involving \"minimum ISBN\" and check the graph relationships.\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_1d7113aec99d4d60b069a120",
